      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/euryrhynchus_amazoniensis_en/",
      "html": "<p>For long-lasting maintenance it needs low pH values and soft water, since otherwise a certain susceptibility to bacterial diseases seems to be present.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/euryrhynchus_amazoniensis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Due to its small size it should naturally not be kept with predatory fish. It is very suitable for a South American community tank with small characins and corys.</p>"
